   <title>org.osgi.service.component.propertytypes</title>
   <info>
      <releaseinfo xml:id="org.osgi.service.component.propertytypes-version">Version 1.5</releaseinfo>
      <edition xml:id="org.osgi.service.component.propertytypes-version.number">1.5</edition>
   </info>
   <para>
Component Property Types Package Version 1.5.
 </para>
   <para>
 When used as annotations, component property types are processed by tools to
 generate Component Descriptions which are used at runtime.
 </para>
   <para>
 Bundles wishing to use this package at runtime must list the package in the
 Import-Package header of the bundle's manifest.
 </para>
   <para>
 Example import for consumers using the API in this package:
 </para>
   <para>
      <code> Import-Package: org.osgi.service.component.propertytypes; version="[1.5,2.0)"</code>
   </para>
   <section role="summary">
      <title>Summary</title>
      <itemizedlist>
         <listitem>
            <para>
               <link linkend="org.osgi.service.component.propertytypes.ExportedService">
                  <code>ExportedService</code>
               </link> - 
Component Property Type for the remote service properties for an exported
 service.
   </para>
         </listitem>
         <listitem>
            <para>
               <link linkend="org.osgi.service.component.propertytypes.SatisfyingConditionTarget">
                  <code>SatisfyingConditionTarget</code>
               </link> - 
Component Property Type for the <code>osgi.ds.satisfying.condition.target</code>
 reference property.
   </para>
         </listitem>
         <listitem>
            <para>
               <link linkend="org.osgi.service.component.propertytypes.ServiceDescription">
                  <code>ServiceDescription</code>
               </link> - 
Component Property Type for the <code>service.description</code> service property.
   </para>
         </listitem>
         <listitem>
            <para>
               <link linkend="org.osgi.service.component.propertytypes.ServiceRanking">
                  <code>ServiceRanking</code>
               </link> - 
Component Property Type for the <code>service.ranking</code> service property.
   </para>
         </listitem>
         <listitem>
            <para>
               <link linkend="org.osgi.service.component.propertytypes.ServiceVendor">
                  <code>ServiceVendor</code>
               </link> - 
Component Property Type for the <code>service.vendor</code> service property.
   </para>
         </listitem>
      </itemizedlist>
   </section>
   <section xreflabel="ExportedService"
            role="class"
            xml:id="org.osgi.service.component.propertytypes.ExportedService">
      <title>@ExportedService</title>
      <para>
Component Property Type for the remote service properties for an exported
 service.
 </para>
      <para>
 This annotation can be used on a <link linkend="org.osgi.service.component.annotations.Component">Component</link> to declare the values of
 the remote service properties for an exported service.</para>
      <formalpara role="parameter">
         <title>See Also</title>
         <para>
            <code>Component Property Types</code>, <code>Remote Services Specification</code>
         </para>
      </formalpara>
      <formalpara role="parameter">
         <title>Since</title>
         <para>1.4</para>
      </formalpara>
      <formalpara role="parameter">
         <title>Retention</title>
         <para>
            <code>CLASS</code>
         </para>
      </formalpara>
      <formalpara role="parameter">
         <title>Target</title>
         <para>
            <code>TYPE</code>
         </para>
      </formalpara>
      <section xreflabel="service_exported_interfaces"
               role="method"
               xml:id="org.osgi.service.component.propertytypes.ExportedService.service_exported_interfaces--">
         <title>Class&lt;?&gt;[] service_exported_interfaces</title>
         <para role="description">
Service property marking the service for export. It defines the
 interfaces under which the service can be exported.
 </para>
         <para>
 If an empty array is specified, the property is not added to the
 component description.</para>
         <formalpara role="parameter">
            <title>Returns</title>
            <para>The exported service interfaces.</para>
         </formalpara>
         <formalpara role="parameter">
            <title>See Also</title>
            <para>
               <link linkend="org.osgi.framework.Constants.SERVICE_EXPORTED_INTERFACES">Constants.SERVICE_EXPORTED_INTERFACES</link>
            </para>
         </formalpara>
      </section>
      <section xreflabel="service_exported_configs"
               role="method"
               xml:id="org.osgi.service.component.propertytypes.ExportedService.service_exported_configs--">
         <title>String[] service_exported_configs default {}</title>
         <para role="description">
Service property identifying the configuration types that should be used
 to export the service.
 </para>
         <para>
 If an empty array is specified, the default value, the property is not
 added to the component description.</para>
         <formalpara role="parameter">
            <title>Returns</title>
            <para>The configuration types.</para>
         </formalpara>
         <formalpara role="parameter">
            <title>See Also</title>
            <para>
               <link linkend="org.osgi.framework.Constants.SERVICE_EXPORTED_CONFIGS">Constants.SERVICE_EXPORTED_CONFIGS</link>
            </para>
         </formalpara>
      </section>
      <section xreflabel="service_exported_intents"
               role="method"
               xml:id="org.osgi.service.component.propertytypes.ExportedService.service_exported_intents--">
         <title>String[] service_exported_intents default {}</title>
         <para role="description">
Service property identifying the intents that the distribution provider
 must implement to distribute the service.
 </para>
         <para>
 If an empty array is specified, the default value, the property is not
 added to the component description.</para>
         <formalpara role="parameter">
            <title>Returns</title>
            <para>The intents that the distribution provider must implement to
         distribute the service.</para>
         </formalpara>
         <formalpara role="parameter">
            <title>See Also</title>
            <para>
               <link linkend="org.osgi.framework.Constants.SERVICE_EXPORTED_INTENTS">Constants.SERVICE_EXPORTED_INTENTS</link>
            </para>
         </formalpara>
      </section>
      <section xreflabel="service_exported_intents_extra"
               role="method"
               xml:id="org.osgi.service.component.propertytypes.ExportedService.service_exported_intents_extra--">
         <title>String[] service_exported_intents_extra default {}</title>
         <para role="description">
Service property identifying the extra intents that the distribution
 provider must implement to distribute the service.
 </para>
         <para>
 If an empty array is specified, the default value, the property is not
 added to the component description.</para>
         <formalpara role="parameter">
            <title>Returns</title>
            <para>The extra intents that the distribution provider must implement
         to distribute the service.</para>
         </formalpara>
         <formalpara role="parameter">
            <title>See Also</title>
            <para>
               <link linkend="org.osgi.framework.Constants.SERVICE_EXPORTED_INTENTS_EXTRA">Constants.SERVICE_EXPORTED_INTENTS_EXTRA</link>
            </para>
         </formalpara>
      </section>
      <section xreflabel="service_intents"
               role="method"
               xml:id="org.osgi.service.component.propertytypes.ExportedService.service_intents--">
         <title>String[] service_intents default {}</title>
         <para role="description">
Service property identifying the intents that this service implements.
 </para>
         <para>
 If an empty array is specified, the default value, the property is not
 added to the component description.</para>
         <formalpara role="parameter">
            <title>Returns</title>
            <para>The intents that the service implements.</para>
         </formalpara>
         <formalpara role="parameter">
            <title>See Also</title>
            <para>
               <link linkend="org.osgi.framework.Constants.SERVICE_INTENTS">Constants.SERVICE_INTENTS</link>
            </para>
         </formalpara>
      </section>
   </section>
   <section xreflabel="SatisfyingConditionTarget"
            role="class"
            xml:id="org.osgi.service.component.propertytypes.SatisfyingConditionTarget">
      <title>@SatisfyingConditionTarget</title>
      <para>
Component Property Type for the <code>osgi.ds.satisfying.condition.target</code>
 reference property.
 </para>
      <para>
 This annotation can be used on a <link linkend="org.osgi.service.component.annotations.Component">Component</link> to declare the value of
 the target property for the component's satisfying condition reference if a
 value other than the default value is desired.</para>
      <formalpara role="parameter">
         <title>See Also</title>
         <para>
            <code>Component Property Types</code>
         </para>
      </formalpara>
      <formalpara role="parameter">
         <title>Since</title>
         <para>1.5</para>
      </formalpara>
      <formalpara role="parameter">
         <title>Retention</title>
         <para>
            <code>CLASS</code>
         </para>
      </formalpara>
      <formalpara role="parameter">
         <title>Target</title>
         <para>
            <code>TYPE</code>
         </para>
      </formalpara>
      <section xreflabel="value"
               role="method"
               xml:id="org.osgi.service.component.propertytypes.SatisfyingConditionTarget.value--">
         <title>String value default "(osgi.condition.id=true)"</title>
         <para role="description">
Filter expression to select the component's satisfying condition.
   </para>
         <formalpara role="parameter">
            <title>Returns</title>
            <para>The filter expression to select the component's satisfying
         condition.</para>
         </formalpara>
      </section>
      <section xreflabel="PREFIX_"
               role="field"
               xml:id="org.osgi.service.component.propertytypes.SatisfyingConditionTarget.PREFIX_">
         <title>String PREFIX_ = "osgi.ds."</title>
         <para>
Prefix for the property name. This value is prepended to each property
 name.
   </para>
      </section>
   </section>
